course: dictionary
lesson: 371
title: A hard word: antisemitism
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Antisemitism is a hard word, and it is important to understand it. It means hatred of, prejudice against or unfair treatment of Jewish people because they are Jewish. Prejudice means judging someone before you know them, just because of who they are.
explain: Read the words around it to help you. «Antisemitism is hatred of Jewish people; it led to the Holocaust, in which about six million Jews were murdered.» The words hatred of Jewish people tell you what it is, and the Holocaust shows how terrible it can become.
explain: Citizenship lessons teach that antisemitism is a form of racism and is wrong. Laws protect people from it. Pupils learn to stand up against it, and to speak out if they hear «antisemitic remarks».
fact: Antisemitism means hatred of, prejudice against or unfair treatment of Jewish people because they are Jewish.
fact: Jewish people are people who follow the Jewish religion or come from Jewish families and culture.
fact: The Holocaust was when the Nazis murdered millions of Jews. About six million Jews were murdered.
fact: Antisemitism is a form of racism, and it is wrong.
fact: To stand up against antisemitism means to speak out, and to refuse to join in with hatred or mocking.
exercise: «Antisemitism is hatred of Jewish people; it led to the Holocaust.» What does antisemitism mean? | Liking and praising people of every faith | A holiday to celebrate a school | *Hatred of, or unfair treatment of, Jewish people because they are Jewish | Being very good at history
exercise: «News reports said antisemitism, hate against Jewish people, rose sharply in many countries.» Which words explain what antisemitism is? | *hate against Jewish people | rose sharply | many countries | News reports
exercise: Why is antisemitism wrong? | Because the law says it is a hobby | Because it is funny to tease people | *Because it is a form of racism and it hurts people | Because it only matters in history lessons
test: «Stand up against antisemitism» means what? | *Speak out and refuse to join in with hatred of Jewish people | Stand still and say nothing | Stand on a chair to be seen | Join in with the mocking
test: According to the lesson, how many Jews were murdered in the Holocaust? | About six | *About six million | Only a few hundred | Ten
exam: Why should a good person never join in with «antisemitic remarks»? | *Because they are hurtful hatred of Jewish people, and they are wrong | Because Jewish people enjoy them | Because remarks like these are never heard by anyone | Because they are funny jokes
